---
/**
 * The shop's one script.
 *
 * The basket count in the header, adding to the basket on a product page,
 * drawing the basket page and emptying the basket after payment are one
 * bundle. Each part starts only when its own markup is on the page, so the same
 * file serves every page of the shop.
 *
 * WHY ONE FILE
 *
 * Astro bundles each component's script separately, and a module that two of
 * them import is split out into a file of its own. The browser only finds that
 * file once the script importing it has arrived, so each split costs a network
 * round trip on a slow connection. A product page with something on sale loaded
 * two scripts and two split files behind them. Under the CI's Lighthouse
 * settings its largest paint went from 2039ms to 1912ms when the four scripts
 * became one, against a budget of 2000ms.
 *
 * So the modules beside this file are imported here and by each other, and
 * nowhere else in client code. `npm run check:bundles` fails if any script a
 * built page loads imports a file of its own.
 *
 * Render it from anything that needs the shop's behaviour. Astro includes a
 * component's script once per page, however many times the component is used.
 */
---

<script>
  import './basket-count';
  import './add-to-basket';
  import './basket-page';
  import './order-complete';
</script>
